Backlog = INTEG(Arrival Rate-Inspection Rate, Initial Backlog)
~ requests
~ Stock: requests waiting for workers to inspect the hot-water problem.
|
Arrival Rate = Base Arrival Rate*Load Multiplier
~ requests/day
~ Inflow of new resident requests. Base rate is an illustrative assumption.
|
Potential Inspection Rate = Backlog/Service Delay
~ requests/day
~ First-order delayed response: larger delay lowers the rate at which the queue is processed.
|
Inspection Rate = MIN(Potential Inspection Rate, Inspection Capacity)
~ requests/day
~ Outflow; bounded by available inspection capacity.
|
Base Arrival Rate = 10
~ requests/day
~ Assumed; no measured request count was provided.
|
Inspection Capacity = 15
~ requests/day
~ Assumed; no staffing or throughput data was provided.
|
Initial Backlog = 20
~ requests
~ Assumed initial queue; no queue count was observed.
|
Base Service Delay = 2
~ day
~ Approximation from the reported "couple of days" until workers arrived to inspect; based on one recollection, not a measured average.
|
Load Multiplier = 1
~ dmnl
~ Set to 2 for the doubled-load scenario.
|
Delay Multiplier = 1
~ dmnl
~ Set to 2 for the doubled-delay scenario.
|
Service Delay = Base Service Delay*Delay Multiplier
~ day
~ First-order response time.
|
INITIAL TIME = 0
~ day
~ |
FINAL TIME = 30
~ day
~ |
TIME STEP = 0.25
~ day
~ |
SAVEPER = TIME STEP
~ day
~ |
